Inequality~(ef{eq-prop-eq-bound-c-step-0}) means that if $c$ denoting $ rac{1}{p n \Delta}$ satisfies  egin{align} 	extstyle{c \geq \left[  rac{2\mu}{\ln (\mu / 
u)} +  rac{\mu}{\Delta}ight] \cdot \left(1+ rac{\delta_5 \iffalse_7  i }{\ln  rac{\mu}{
u} - \delta_5 \iffalse_7  i }ight) ,} \end{align} where $\delta_5$ satisfies $0<\delta_5 \iffalse_7  i < \ln  rac{\mu}{
u}$ (i.e., Inequality~(ef{eq-define-delta_2-upperbound})), then Inequality~(ef{eq-c-lower-bound-prop-eq-bound-c-step-1}) follows. Thus, under Inequality~(ef{eq-define-delta_2-upperbound}), we have  egin{align} 	extup{Inequality~(ef{eq-c-lower-bound-prop-eq-bound-c-step-1})} \xLeftarrow{	extup{Lemma~ef{prop-eq-bound-c-step-0}}}	extup{Inequality~(ef{eq-c-lower-bound-prop-eq-bound-c-step-0})} . \end{align}

